<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes:ttttt  n1. The Board has recommended a dividend of Rs.4 per Equity Share of Rs.10/- for FY 2019-20.  ntttt  n2. Sugar production being seasonal, performance of one quarter is not indicative of the trend for the whole year.tttt  n  n3. Figures for the last quarter are the difference between the audited figures for the full financial year and the published figures for nine months period upto the third quarter of relevant financial year.tttt  n  n4. Figures for the previous period have been regrouped wherever necessary.tttt  nttttt  n5. Exceptional items comprise of: (Rs. in Lakhs)tQuarter endedtYear endedttttttttt31-03-2020ttt  nt - Write back under Indirect taxes settlement schemet(53)t(53)tt  n  n6. Undue delay in realising dues pertaining to power sales continues to strain liquidity and credit rating.tttt  n  n7. Production operations remained shut between 25-03-2020 and 21-04-2020 due to Covid-19 induced lockdown and consequent disruption. This pushed tail end crushing to summer months, depressing sugar recovery. The Company incurs higher compliance cost to conform to SOPs under Covid Guidelines. Sugar prices face bearish pressures under adverse market. All these have a negative financial impact on the Company the extent of which is not readily quantifiable. The Company however is hopeful of weathering these challenges.tttt  n  n8. The above financial results were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at the respective meetings held on 29th May 2020.tttt  nttttttFor Ponni Sugars ( Erode) Ltdttt  nttttt  nChennaitttttttN Ramanathantt  n29.05.2020ttttt             Managing Director</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
